## 30. FINAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is complete only when the following core workflows work end to end:

WORKFLOW A — REGISTRATION:
A new user registers → Firebase Authentication creates the account → Firestore stores the appropriate profile → the user logs in → the dashboard displays the user's actual information.

WORKFLOW B — PROFILE UPDATE:
The user edits their profile → the backend or authorized Firestore operation validates the update → the information is saved → the updated information appears after refreshing.

WORKFLOW C — COURSE MANAGEMENT:
An authorized administrator creates a course → the backend verifies admin permission → Firestore stores the course → the administrator publishes it → the public Courses page displays it.

WORKFLOW D — USER PERSONALIZATION:
The user enters skills and career interests → the recommendation engine analyzes them → suitable catalog careers are suggested → missing skills are identified → a personalized roadmap is saved → the dashboard displays the saved roadmap.

WORKFLOW E — AI RESUME ANALYSIS:
The user uploads a private resume → the backend processes it securely → Gemini produces a validated analysis → the user sees the result → the private analysis is saved to the user's records.

WORKFLOW F — SECURITY:
A normal user cannot administer courses, access another user's private profile, retrieve another user's resume, or grant themselves administrator privileges.

WORKFLOW G — DEPLOYMENT:
The frontend is deployed, backend functions are configured, Firebase rules are deployed, environment variables and secrets are configured, and the core workflows have been tested against the deployed application.

